# Flag 2 – Return Address Integrity Violation

## Invariant
Functions must return execution only to their legitimate caller
return addresses.

## Telemetry
The binary provides no shadow stack, return address validation, or
control-flow integrity instrumentation. The assessment evaluates
this absence of telemetry.

## Observation
Observed. Return addresses are not validated at runtime, allowing
control flow redirection without crashes or alerts.

## Security Impact
Return address manipulation enables control-flow hijacking that can
alter execution logic while preserving outwardly correct behavior.

## Limitations
No exploit was demonstrated; findings are derived from missing
runtime protections.

